cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "gz_ecm_battery_plugin: A Chemistry-Agnostic Equivalent-Circuit Battery Plugin for Gazebo Sim"
authors:
  - family-names: "Ponguillo-Intriago"
    given-names: "Ronald"
    email: "ronald.ponguilloi@ug.edu.ec"
    affiliation: "Facultad de Ciencias Matematicas y Fisicas, Universidad de Guayaquil"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7554-8367"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-04"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A chemistry-agnostic Equivalent-Circuit-Model (ECM) battery plugin for Gazebo
  Sim, implementing Plett's Enhanced Self-Correcting model: a user-supplied
  non-linear OCV(SOC) curve, series resistance, one or two RC polarization
  branches and hysteresis, all declared from SDF so that modelling a different
  cell requires no recompilation. Validated against three independent public
  datasets (Panasonic 18650PF, LG 18650HG2, Molicel INR-21700-P42A) at
  33-34 mV RMSE, and across -20 to 25 degrees Celsius.
repository-code: "https://github.com/rponguil/gz_ecm_battery_plugin"
keywords:
  - gazebo
  - ros2
  - battery model
  - equivalent circuit model
  - robotics simulation
  - unmanned aerial vehicle
references:
  - type: book
    authors:
      - family-names: "Plett"
        given-names: "Gregory L."
    title: "Battery Management Systems, Volume 1: Battery Modeling"
    publisher:
      name: "Artech House"
    year: 2015
